==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{term|ad||towards|lang=la}}; ''axis'' axis

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{botany}} On the side that is [[towards]] the [[axis]] or central line, usually on the [[upper]] side.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae V|4}}
#*: {{...}}it has been transformed, except in a few taxa where lobules are always explanate, into a galeate water-sac, which is formed wholly from the lobule, with the external surface from the '''adaxial''' leaf surface.
# (''developmental biology'') Paraxial mesoderm cells adjacent to the axis, or in vertebrates the notochord. In zebrafish, the adaxial cells are precursors to the embryonic slow muscle fibers.  Their development into slow muscle fibers is dependent on Hedgehog signaling from the notochord.

